WEBVTT

00:06.690 --> 00:09.100
What were those dogs called again?

00:09.100 --> 00:12.290
The really fluffy kind...

00:13.640 --> 00:15.890
Oh yeah, they're called Pomeranians.

01:49.410 --> 01:50.430
What time is it?

01:50.430 --> 01:51.490
It's Peanut Butter Jelly time,

01:51.490 --> 01:53.480
and it's 11:53...

01:53.480 --> 01:55.590
Well, sometime between 53 and 54,

01:55.590 --> 01:56.890
so I guess around 11:53 and 30 seconds.

01:56.890 --> 01:59.220
Why didn't you keep going with the Peanut Butter Jelly time?

01:59.220 --> 02:00.920
Well, I could have, but...

02:00.920 --> 02:02.800
There you guys are.

02:02.800 --> 02:03.650
He's here.

02:03.650 --> 02:04.580
Mr. Antkiller!

02:04.780 --> 02:05.850
Hello!

02:05.850 --> 02:07.800
I've been looking everywhere for you guys.

02:07.800 --> 02:10.850
I thought you guys would sit in the non-smoking seats, not the smoking ones.

02:13.860 --> 02:17.270
Why did you guys pick the smoking seats?

02:17.830 --> 02:19.420
But I thought you smoked, Mr. Antkiller—

02:19.420 --> 02:22.480
That kind of "thinking" won't get you anywhere, punk.

02:22.480 --> 02:25.900
I quit smoking.

02:25.900 --> 02:27.590
I thought I told you guys last time.

02:28.990 --> 02:30.120
We must have missed it.

02:30.120 --> 02:32.430
Are you sure you weren't telling some other monster?

02:32.430 --> 02:33.660
Well, forget it.

02:33.660 --> 02:35.210
Let's move to the non-smoking seats.

02:35.210 --> 02:36.490
Bring the waters.

02:36.840 --> 02:37.600
Okay.

02:37.600 --> 02:39.660
Don't we have to tell them we're moving first?

02:39.660 --> 02:41.990
It'll be fine. We'll just tell them when we get there.

02:44.320 --> 02:45.820
What would you like to order, Mr. Antkiller?

02:45.820 --> 02:47.940
Let me see...

02:48.220 --> 02:50.430
It looks like lunch meals here come with salad bar access.

02:50.430 --> 02:52.780
You like vegetables, don't you, Mr. Antkiller?

02:52.780 --> 02:56.570
I guess spaghetti sounds okay, good ol' ghetti.

02:56.570 --> 02:58.170
But then again,

02:58.170 --> 02:59.860
you can buy ghetti from convenience stores too,

02:59.860 --> 03:02.770
so maybe it's not worth ordering from a restaurant.

03:02.770 --> 03:04.330
What should I get...

03:04.330 --> 03:06.220
"Ghetti..."?

03:06.930 --> 03:08.610
They have a salad bar here.

03:09.980 --> 03:11.530
You know,

03:11.530 --> 03:15.620
I might have been adamant about getting a salad last time we were here,

03:15.620 --> 03:18.230
but that doesn't mean you should automatically assume

03:18.230 --> 03:21.130
and think that I like salads.

03:21.850 --> 03:25.710
Little did you know, I ordered a salad last time out of mortal necessity,

03:25.710 --> 03:28.220
and not because I like salads or anything.

03:28.220 --> 03:29.440
It was a one time thing.

03:29.440 --> 03:31.470
A mortal necessity born from not eating enough vegetables.

03:31.930 --> 03:34.170
So I'm sorry, but I don't feel like eating a salad today.

03:34.170 --> 03:35.260
I see.

03:34.870 --> 03:36.520
What should I get?

03:36.520 --> 03:38.450
What should <i>we </i> get then?

03:38.450 --> 03:40.940
Yeah, good question.

03:40.940 --> 03:42.380
I think I'll get the Salisbury Steak Lunch.

03:42.380 --> 03:44.010
I'll take the Pork Cutlet Lunch then.

03:43.520 --> 03:45.120
I'll get...

03:45.120 --> 03:47.120
the Ginger Chicken Lunch.

03:47.810 --> 03:48.520
Um...

03:48.520 --> 03:49.020
What?

03:49.020 --> 03:50.640
The lunch sets here come with salad bar—

03:50.640 --> 03:52.200
I don't <i>have </i> to use the salad bar, right?

03:52.200 --> 03:53.880
You got a problem with that?

03:54.130 --> 03:55.300
No...

03:55.300 --> 03:56.640
Thank you for waiting!

03:56.640 --> 03:58.800
Here are your plates for the salad bar.

03:58.800 --> 04:01.560
We're going to head over to the salad bar.

04:01.560 --> 04:02.870
Sure, go ahead.

04:14.550 --> 04:15.910
They have tomatoes!

04:16.210 --> 04:17.400
I'll have some tomatoes.

04:17.400 --> 04:18.940
You really love those tomatoes, don't you.

04:18.940 --> 04:20.390
You guys are too slow!

04:21.450 --> 04:24.650
How dare you make me wait for over a minute?

04:24.650 --> 04:25.570
S-Sorry!

04:25.570 --> 04:27.970
You didn't have to hit me with your main weapon...

04:27.970 --> 04:29.830
What the hell, tomatoes again?

04:29.830 --> 04:31.120
You really like them, huh?

04:32.770 --> 04:35.710
Woah, they have potato salad!

04:36.530 --> 04:37.980
Oh, you're right.

04:38.230 --> 04:40.910
Why didn't you guys tell me they had potato salad here?

04:41.730 --> 04:44.140
I'll go get you your salad plate, Mr. Antkiller!

04:44.140 --> 04:45.510
We're really sorry.

04:45.510 --> 04:46.720
I just now noticed it's there—

04:46.720 --> 04:49.120
Notice faster next time, punk!

04:49.120 --> 04:51.390
Potato salad's like one of my favorites you know.

04:51.390 --> 04:52.280
Mr. Antkiller!

04:52.280 --> 04:54.240
They brought over your rice and soup to the table already.

04:54.240 --> 04:56.050
For reals? Let's hurry it up then.

04:56.050 --> 04:57.010
Okay.

05:23.990 --> 05:25.950
Here's your Ginger Chicken.

05:25.950 --> 05:29.130
When did you quit smoking?

05:29.130 --> 05:31.610
It's only been two days so far.

05:31.610 --> 05:33.280
Don't you get the urge to smoke, then?

05:33.280 --> 05:35.560
My life depends on it.

05:35.560 --> 05:38.900
I actually had my big brother put a no-smoking curse on me.

05:38.900 --> 05:40.970
Your big brother? You have a brother?

05:40.970 --> 05:42.640
Didn't you know?

05:42.640 --> 05:44.210
Mr. Antkiller is related to

05:44.210 --> 05:45.080
Mr. Khamenman.

05:45.980 --> 05:47.120
Really?

05:47.120 --> 05:48.400
Yeah.

05:48.400 --> 05:51.540
Now that you mention it, I guess you two kind of look alike.

05:51.900 --> 05:53.750
What are you laughing about?

05:53.750 --> 05:54.660
Oh, nothing.

05:54.660 --> 05:58.150
That means both you and Mr. Khamenman have been around for at least 4000 years,

05:58.150 --> 06:00.140
and you guys are only two years apart, right?

06:00.140 --> 06:01.600
What's so funny about that?

06:01.600 --> 06:04.980
I just thought two years out of 4000 isn't long enough a headstart for you to be calling him "big brother."

06:04.980 --> 06:06.720
It seems like you guys are kinda stingy about it all.

06:06.720 --> 06:07.480
Isn't it stingy?

06:07.480 --> 06:08.870
You have a point there.

06:10.010 --> 06:12.010
Shut up about it already.

06:12.810 --> 06:15.080
So what's this "no-smoking curse" you mentioned?

06:15.380 --> 06:17.570
I'll become cursed the moment I smoke a cigarette.

06:17.570 --> 06:19.890
Apparently I'll start bleeding out if I do.

06:20.150 --> 06:21.290
Bleed out?

06:21.290 --> 06:22.310
That's scary.

06:22.310 --> 06:23.900
I guess you really shouldn't smoke then.

06:23.900 --> 06:25.190
Don't you think so?

06:25.190 --> 06:28.780
I have to quit smoking since my life literally depends on it.

06:30.760 --> 06:33.090
May I take the plates you're finished with?

06:33.990 --> 06:35.730
Give me some coffee.

06:35.730 --> 06:37.830
Lunch sets come with unlimited refills for coffee, right?

06:37.830 --> 06:40.800
I ordered black tea, so I can't get more coffee.

06:40.800 --> 06:41.670
We shouldn't be doing that.

06:41.670 --> 06:43.150
What <i>should </i> we do then?

06:43.150 --> 06:44.870
You guys can just go get another cup.

06:44.870 --> 06:46.330
That counts as a petty crime, you know.

06:46.330 --> 06:47.970
They'll arrest you if they find out.

06:47.970 --> 06:50.510
You really think we're going to get arrested?

06:50.510 --> 06:53.310
You're a monster, so you should know better, you idiot.

06:53.310 --> 06:53.530
But—

06:53.530 --> 06:56.190
Forget about it, we just won't come back here anymore.

06:56.190 --> 06:57.840
But we're regulars here...

06:57.840 --> 06:59.020
Yeah.

07:01.150 --> 07:02.540
Let me take your water glasses for you.

07:03.880 --> 07:05.350
I'm full.

07:05.350 --> 07:06.810
What should we do next?

07:06.810 --> 07:07.440
Do you want to watch a movie?

07:07.440 --> 07:08.210
A movie?

07:08.210 --> 07:09.230
Oh yeah,

07:09.230 --> 07:11.430
are they still playing that "Warman" or whatever?

07:11.430 --> 07:13.590
I'm not sure...

07:13.590 --> 07:15.380
M-Mr. Antkiller!

07:15.380 --> 07:16.990
You're... You're smoking!

07:16.990 --> 07:17.580
He's right!

07:17.580 --> 07:18.780
Oh shit!

07:18.780 --> 07:22.550
I'm so used to smoking after meals that I just did it automatically!

07:22.550 --> 07:23.930
I'm fucked.

07:23.930 --> 07:26.420
M-Mr. Antkiller?

07:27.230 --> 07:30.670
You're not really bleeding out or anything.

07:31.850 --> 07:33.880
You really believed that?

07:33.880 --> 07:34.850
Dumbass.

07:34.850 --> 07:38.130
Why would the Ancient Egyptians have a curse against smoking?

07:38.130 --> 07:41.290
How dare you trick me!

07:41.290 --> 07:43.610
It's the dumbass brothers who argue about seniority when they're both over 4000 years old!

07:43.610 --> 07:46.850
I wasn't doing it to help you quit smoking though.

07:46.850 --> 07:49.200
Quit fucking with me, bro!

07:49.200 --> 07:51.880
Well I just did, bro!

08:00.960 --> 08:02.980
The Animal Soldiers' mission this time

08:02.980 --> 08:04.370
was a random intrusion—

08:04.370 --> 08:06.520
I mean, a routine breaking-in to Red's home.

08:06.520 --> 08:08.730
It just won't open.

08:08.730 --> 08:11.020
I guess we have no choice but to break the door down.

08:11.020 --> 08:14.030
We can't do that, Kayoko lives here!

08:16.830 --> 08:18.220
You'll open it, you say?

08:18.220 --> 08:20.370
Don't break the door down, okay?

08:23.730 --> 08:26.290
L-Liquid metal?

08:36.270 --> 08:38.690
I heard sushi boat is really good, Usa.

08:38.690 --> 08:41.180
But isn't it expensive?

08:41.830 --> 08:43.050
I heard it's cheap.

08:43.050 --> 08:43.760
Really?

08:43.760 --> 08:45.130
Let's go, then.

08:46.280 --> 08:47.320
Welcome.

08:47.320 --> 08:48.310
We're at the right place, right?

08:48.630 --> 08:50.440
I don't see boats though.

08:50.440 --> 08:52.260
I wonder why.

08:52.320 --> 08:54.520
They're probably cheaper since they're not on boats, then.

08:54.520 --> 08:56.890
You're right, let's dig in!

08:59.460 --> 09:01.600
That was so good!

09:01.600 --> 09:03.550
I'm so full.

09:03.880 --> 09:06.150
I should have thought about my diabetes before eating.

09:06.880 --> 09:09.320
That'll be 420 dollars, please.

09:11.040 --> 09:12.010
What should we do?

09:12.010 --> 09:13.500
I only have thirty cents.

09:13.500 --> 09:15.090
I only have sixty.

09:15.090 --> 09:17.970
They wouldn't have had enough money even if they <i>were</i> at a sushi boat place!

09:17.970 --> 09:19.140
What about you, P-chan?

09:19.140 --> 09:21.200
ZERO!

09:24.330 --> 09:26.970
No fair.

09:27.310 --> 09:28.540
What?

09:28.540 --> 09:30.980
Did you guy walk in here and eat sushi without any money?

09:30.980 --> 09:32.850
We're so sorry!

09:32.850 --> 09:34.570
We didn't mean to.

09:34.570 --> 09:36.180
Bang!

09:36.180 --> 09:38.300
T-Too cute!

09:38.300 --> 09:39.790
All right,

09:39.790 --> 09:42.330
you don't have to pay this time.

09:42.330 --> 09:43.640
Really?

09:43.640 --> 09:45.830
Yeah, but in exchange...

09:45.830 --> 09:47.330
Come eat sushi here everyday,

09:47.330 --> 09:49.040
you don't need to pay.

09:49.600 --> 09:53.000
I usually wolf down boiled eggs for lunch.

09:53.000 --> 09:55.180
Sunny side up is good, too.

09:55.920 --> 09:57.080
Sushi for lunch again?

09:57.380 --> 09:59.550
This can't be good for my cholesterol.

10:02.160 --> 10:04.070
They're actually baddies.

10:07.770 --> 10:10.260
Do you have a girlfriend, Number One?

10:10.260 --> 10:11.290
I do.

10:11.290 --> 10:12.510
I had no idea.

10:12.510 --> 10:15.290
We're actually in a long-distance relationship.

10:14.910 --> 10:15.290
From where to where?

10:15.290 --> 10:17.400
Astro Fighter Sunred's Theme Song!

10:15.690 --> 10:17.400
Shinagawa to Omiya I guess...

10:17.400 --> 10:19.670
Sunred's Theme!

10:19.750 --> 10:22.130
Pa Pa Pa Paa Paa Paa (Fuwa Fuwa)

10:22.420 --> 10:25.470
Pa Pa Pa Paa Paa Paa (Fuwa Fuwa)

10:25.770 --> 10:27.900
Who could that be?

10:28.480 --> 10:30.740
Who could that be?

10:31.720 --> 10:35.590
His mask shines brilliantly in red.

10:35.670 --> 10:37.010
(What's it made of?)

10:37.150 --> 10:40.200
He shines the light of justice on the world.

10:40.400 --> 10:42.650
(Especially Kanagawa.)

10:43.280 --> 10:46.280
Astro Fighter Sunred.

10:46.450 --> 10:48.190
(Sunred.)

10:48.830 --> 10:51.120
The terrifying organization known as Florsheim

10:51.580 --> 10:53.960
are his enemies.

10:54.290 --> 10:57.020
General Vamp is the devil's minion.

10:57.250 --> 10:58.960
He's really "that."

10:59.320 --> 11:00.520
You better watch out.

11:00.550 --> 11:01.890
(What exactly is "that"?)

11:02.280 --> 11:06.510
Find the Sunshoot.

11:08.060 --> 11:11.670
It was inside a toolbox two years ago.

11:11.700 --> 11:13.620
(Along with carpentry tools!)

11:13.780 --> 11:18.040
Find the Sunshoot.

11:19.500 --> 11:22.920
The insides of the drawer look suspicious!!

11:22.920 --> 11:25.810
(If it's not there it's probably on the top drawer of the shoe stack!)

11:26.070 --> 11:30.340
You're amazing.

11:30.340 --> 11:32.140
Our one and only...

11:32.210 --> 11:34.540
Ceiling!

11:35.250 --> 11:37.460
Pa Pa Pa Paa Paa Paa

11:37.460 --> 11:38.430
Verse two!

11:38.580 --> 11:40.640
Who could that be?

11:41.230 --> 11:43.420
Who could that be?

11:44.310 --> 11:48.650
Who's that red guy who wakes up at noon?

11:48.650 --> 11:49.830
(It's because he's a you-know-what.)

11:49.830 --> 11:53.140
He shines the light of justice on the world.

11:53.180 --> 11:55.720
(Especially Kawasaki City in Kanagawa.)

11:56.100 --> 11:59.170
Astro Fighter Sunred.

11:59.170 --> 12:01.150
(Sunred.)

12:01.500 --> 12:04.150
His girlfriend, Kayoko, is almost thirty,

12:04.230 --> 12:07.610
and works at an insurance firm.

12:07.650 --> 12:09.700
(She gets paid on commission.)

12:10.030 --> 12:13.680
Go go Florsheim!

12:15.740 --> 12:18.710
Florsheim's actually very "that."

12:18.710 --> 12:21.250
(What's this "that" you keep talking about?!)

12:21.510 --> 12:25.140
Go go Florsheim!

12:27.250 --> 12:30.270
Proceed with Plan A.

12:30.270 --> 12:32.710
(Except on rainy days.)

12:33.250 --> 12:34.240
You really are

12:34.290 --> 12:37.430
really amazing.

12:37.500 --> 12:39.380
Our one and only...

12:39.380 --> 12:43.870
Ceiling!

12:44.220 --> 12:46.340
Go for the 78th spot on the Billboard chart!

12:46.340 --> 12:48.380
78th!

12:50.980 --> 12:52.720
We're really "that"?
